use std
use amni-drive
into cockpit_render.amni
lang amni
Amni-Drive's Helium + Gold software cockpit renderer and desktop preview generator. Draws any `layout::CockpitPlan` and `look::Palette` into an RGBA byte buffer (`w * h * 4` bytes, row-major R, G, B, A) using clean anti-aliased signed-distance primitives, compass ticks, chamfered octagonal polygons, stadium capsules, and a crisp built-in 5x7 pixel-block vector font scaled for high-legibility car displays.
Struct `Canvas` holds `w` and `h` as 32-bit integers and `px` as a growable byte buffer of length `w * h * 4`.
Function `new_canvas` takes `w` and `h` as 32-bit integers and `bg` as an unsigned 32-bit ARGB color, returning a `Canvas` filled with `bg` (unpacking R, G, B, A).
Function `blend_px` takes a mutable `Canvas` `c`, `x` and `y` as 32-bit integers, `col` as an unsigned 32-bit ARGB color, and `cov` as a 32-bit float coverage in 0 through 1. If `x` or `y` is out of bounds or `cov` is at most 0, return. Compute effective alpha `a = (f32((col >> 24) & 255) / 255.0) * clamp(cov, 0.0, 1.0)` and alpha-blend R, G, B over the destination pixel, keeping destination alpha 255.
Function `fill_round_rect` takes a mutable `Canvas` `c`, `x`, `y`, `w`, `h`, and `radius` as 32-bit floats, `fill` and `stroke` as unsigned 32-bit colors, and `stroke_w` as a 32-bit float. Clamp `radius` to at most `min(w, h) * 0.5`. Iterate integer pixels inside the bounding box expanded by 2 pixels; compute the exact rounded-rectangle signed distance `d` from the box center and half-extents. Fill pixels where `d < 0.5` with smooth 1-pixel anti-aliased coverage `clamp(0.5 - d, 0.0, 1.0)`; if `stroke_w > 0.0` and `stroke` alpha is nonzero, blend `stroke` on the rim where `d` is between `-stroke_w - 0.5` and `0.5`.
Function `fill_circle_pod` takes a mutable `Canvas` `c`, `cx`, `cy`, and `r` as 32-bit floats, `fill` and `stroke` as unsigned 32-bit colors, `stroke_w` as a 32-bit float, and `ticks` as a boolean. Draw an anti-aliased filled circle with stroke ring using Euclidean distance `d = hypot(px - cx, py - cy) - r`. When `ticks` is true, draw 36 radial compass ticks around the inner rim (`r - 10` to `r - 3`, longer every 90 degrees) in `stroke`.
Function `fill_hex_pod` takes a mutable `Canvas` `c`, `x`, `y`, `w`, `h`, and `cut` as 32-bit floats, `fill` and `stroke` as unsigned 32-bit colors, and `stroke_w` as a 32-bit float. Compute the chamfered octagon signed distance as the maximum of the axis-aligned box distance `max(abs(dx) - hw, abs(dy) - hh)` and the 45-degree corner-cut distance `(abs(dx) + abs(dy) - (hw + hh - cut)) * 0.70710678`, and draw anti-aliased fill + stroke rim.
Function `glyph_rows` takes an ASCII byte `ch` and returns a 32-bit unsigned integer packing a 5-wide by 7-tall bitmap (row 0 in bits 0..4, row 1 in bits 5..9, ..., row 6 in bits 30..34 — use a 64-bit unsigned integer so all 35 bits fit cleanly!) for uppercase A through Z, digits 0 through 9, space, colon, degree symbol (or `o` fallback), dot, dash, slash, and plus. Map lowercase `a`..`z` to uppercase.
Function `draw_text` takes a mutable `Canvas` `c`, `text` as a read-only byte slice, `x` and `y` as 32-bit floats, `scale` as a 32-bit integer (minimum 1), `col` as an unsigned 32-bit color, and `center_x` as a boolean. Total width is `text.len * 6 * scale - scale`. If `center_x` is true, shift start `x` left by half of total width. For each character, iterate 7 rows by 5 columns of `glyph_rows(ch)` and fill `scale` by `scale` pixel blocks where the bit is 1.
Function `draw_cockpit` takes `w` and `h` as 32-bit integers, `preset_key` as a read-only byte slice, `layout_id` and `dock_mode` as 32-bit integers, `speed_mph` as a 32-bit integer, `temp_f` as a 32-bit integer, and `active_btn` as a 32-bit integer (1..6), returning a `Canvas`.
Use `look::build_palette(preset_key, 0, false)`, `look::car_type_scale(f32(w), f32(h), 1.0)`, and `layout::compute_cockpit(f32(w), f32(h), ts.min_hit_px, ts.gutter_px, ts.pad_px, layout_id, dock_mode, false)`.
1. Create canvas filled with `pal.bg`.
2. Draw `plan.dock_rect` as a rounded container (`radius = 20`, fill `pal.panel`, stroke `pal.line`, `stroke_w = 1.5`).
3. Draw each of the 6 buttons in `plan.buttons`: labels are `"NAV"`, `"MEDIA"`, `"APPS"`, `"VOICE"`, `"VIEW"`, `"SET"` for ids 1 through 6. For button 4 (`primary` VOICE), draw a glowing circular/pill orb with `pal.acc` ring (`stroke_w = 2.5`) and `pal.panel2` fill (or `pal.acc` fill if active). For the active button (`b.id` equals `active_btn`), fill with `pal.acc` and draw dark/light contrasting text (`0xFF05070A` if dark theme else `0xFFFFFFFF`); otherwise fill `pal.panel2` with `pal.line` stroke and `pal.ink` text. Choose text scale `max(2, int(ts.button_px / 9.0))` centered inside the button.
4. Draw each pod in `plan.pods`:
   - For shape 1 (circle): call `fill_circle_pod` at `pod.circle` with fill `pal.panel`, stroke `pal.acc` if `pod.kind` is 0 (map) else `pal.line2`, `stroke_w` 2.0, and `ticks` true when `pod.kind` is 0 or 2.
   - For shape 2 (hex): call `fill_hex_pod` at `pod.rect` with `pod.chamfer`, fill `pal.panel`, stroke `pal.acc` if `pod.kind` is 0 else `pal.line2`, `stroke_w = 2.0`.
   - For shape 3 (capsule): call `fill_round_rect` at `pod.rect` with `pod.chamfer`, fill `pal.panel`, stroke `pal.acc` if `pod.kind` is 0 else `pal.line2`, `stroke_w = 2.0`.
   - Otherwise (rect): call `fill_round_rect` at `pod.rect` with radius 22, fill `pal.panel`, stroke `pal.acc` if `pod.kind` is 0 else `pal.line2`, `stroke_w = 1.5`.
   - Inside each pod's `safe_rect` center, draw crisp glanceable content:
     - `kind` 0 (map): subtle inner road grid lines in `pal.panel2`, a bold route chevron/bar in `pal.acc`, `"AMNI-MAP 3D"` title, and `"HEADING UP"` subtitle in `pal.soft`.
     - `kind` 1 (media): circular album-art badge in `pal.panel2` with `pal.acc` ring, `"SPOTIFY"` label, track title `"NIGHT DRIVE"`, and large `<<  PLAY  >>` transport bar at bottom of `safe_rect` with `pal.acc` play pill.
     - `kind` 2 (speed): large telemetry number (formatted `speed_mph`, scale `max(3, int(ts.telemetry_px / 10.0))`) in `pal.ink` above `"MPH"` in `pal.acc`.
     - `kind` 3 (weather): large temperature (formatted `temp_f` + `"F"`) in `pal.gold` above `"CLEAR"` in `pal.soft`.
     - `kind` 4 (apps): `"APPS"` + 4 accent orb dots arranged in a ring.
     - `kind` 5 (widgets): stacked `"65 MPH"` + `"72F CLEAR"` + `"11:45 PM"` telemetry cards.
Function `write_ppm` takes a `Canvas` `c` and `path` as a read-only byte slice, and writes a binary P6 PPM image (`"P6\n<w> <h>\n255\n"` followed by RGB bytes) using `std` file I/O.
Function `main` renders four preview images into `/tmp/amni_he_preview/`:
1. `honda_800x480_twin_chrono.ppm` (800 by 480, `"amni_dark"`, layout 0, dock 0, speed 65, temp 72, active 1)
2. `car_1280x720_solar_orbit.ppm` (1280 by 720, `"amni_dark"`, layout 1, dock 0, speed 68, temp 72, active 1)
3. `car_1280x720_hex_light.ppm` (1280 by 720, `"amni_light"`, layout 4, dock 0, speed 45, temp 74, active 2)
4. `portrait_720x1280_capsule.ppm` (720 by 1280, `"high_contrast"`, layout 5, dock 1, speed 55, temp 68, active 1)
Print `"rendered 4 helium previews ok"` when done.
